# Larastan baseline.
#
# Deliberately EMPTY. The 13 entries recorded in 3.2.1 were all fixed at the
# source rather than suppressed:
#
#   - @property annotations on CustomField, Plan, Listing and User declare the
#     attributes whose runtime type comes from casts(); Larastan resolves model
#     properties from annotations, not from the casts array.
#   - SetLocale narrows Auth::user() to the concrete model before reading
#     $locale, which Authenticatable does not declare.
#   - ListingController returns an Eloquent collection, which is what ->get()
#     actually produces.
#   - UpdateCustomField drops the ?? on an option offset the normalised shape
#     guarantees.
#   - AttemptLogin states the nullability whereRaw() loses for the analyser.
#
# Any entry added here must carry `message`, `identifier`, `count` and `path`
# together. Matching on identifier + path alone lets a SECOND error of the same
# kind in the same file pass unnoticed, which defeats the gate; the count is
# what keeps the suppressed set fixed. With reportUnmatchedIgnoredErrors set to
# true in phpstan.neon, an entry whose error has been fixed fails the analysis
# and must be deleted.

parameters:
    ignoreErrors: []
